   "tag": "p",
   "text": "THE CONVERSATION WORKSHOP"
  },
  {
   "tag": "h1",
   "text": "Truthful words. A human conversation."
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "text": "Practise understanding the concern, choosing a first response and putting an answer into your own words."
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "text": "AN IMAGINED CONVERSATION"
  },
  {
   "tag": "h2",
   "text": "“Where was God when I needed him?”"
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "text": "A friend is speaking about a painful loss, not asking for a formal debate."
  },
  {
   "tag": "h3",
   "text": "What would you say first?"
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "text": "A RHYTHM TO RETURN TO"
  },
  {
   "tag": "h2",
   "text": "Listen. Clarify. Give a reason. Invite."
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "text": "An editorial practice pattern drawn from the passages below."
  },
  {
   "tag": "h3",
   "text": "Understand the person before answering the position."
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "text": "Invite them to explain what they believe and why it matters to them. Reflect it back in words they recognise."
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "text": "What has most shaped your understanding of God?"
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "text": "Conviction with an open Bible. Scripture first. Reformed convictions. Sources you can examine."
  },
  {
   "tag": "h2",
   "text": "Rooted in Scripture. Open for discovery."
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "text": "A place to read slowly, ask deeply, and follow the connections. Scripture, study and the voices of Christian history, brought together for a lifetime of learning."
  },
  {
   "tag": "h3",
   "text": "SPEND TIME IN THE WORD"
  },
